silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_02_typed_noun_discipline_sections_01_typed_noun_rule_concrete_anchor_3_DomesticCatBox#domesticcatbox silm:hasLongDescription "The DomesticCatBox is the admitted O_eng object output of tau_N('a domestic cat'). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'DomesticCatBox', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
